---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StataChart from '../components/StataChart.astro';
import StataPlan from '../components/StataPlan.astro';
import { author } from '../data/author';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';

// Numbers that are static README-verbatim text (not in a sidecar), with their
// source in the demo at github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage:
//   TurtleBot3 to Tiago, "fired five times"         README.md, docs/transferability.md
//   recovery_alpha 0.0, the two ros2 param lines    docs/finding-amcl-recovery.md
//   rosbag2 or ROS 1 .bag; reads from disk, calls nothing outside it   README.md
//   wrong corridor                                                      docs/finding-confidently-wrong.md
//   from 2027: Machinery Regulation (EU) 2023/1230, tracing logs from 20 Jan 2027 (EUR-Lex, linked)
// Everything else renders from public/data/*.json, written by
// scripts/sample-stata-replay.py from the demo's results/stata/.
const REPO = 'https://github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage';
const REGULATION = 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32023R1230';
const mailto = `mailto:${author.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('One incident')}`;

const readJson = (f: string) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), 'public/data', f), 'utf8'));
// From the last ceiling-marker pose on floor 2 to the first one after the robot came back.
const { zones_s } = readJson('stata-replay.meta.json') as { zones_s: { healthy_end_s: number; lost_start_s: number } };
const offMapMinutes = ['one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five'][Math.round((zones_s.lost_start_s - zones_s.healthy_end_s) / 60) - 1];
const base = readJson('stata-baseline.json') as {
  sigma_hindsight: { lost: number; healthy: number };
  detectors: { lost: number; healthy: number };
  detectors_events_starting_in_lost_window: number;
  lost_by_neither_hindsight: number;
};
if (base.sigma_hindsight.healthy !== base.detectors.healthy) {
  throw new Error('stata-baseline.json: the comparison is only fair at an equal healthy flag rate');
}
---

<BaseLayout ogType="profile">
  <main class="page">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="who">
        <strong>Théo Hermann</strong>, independent practitioner. MSc Robotics, EPFL. Perception and autonomy work at EPFL VITA Lab, IRI Barcelona and Roboat, 2022 to 2024.
      </p>
      <h1>When an autonomous robot fails in ways your logs don't explain, I find the real cause and prove it, independently.</h1>
      <div class="hero-side">
        <p class="lede">
          Your tools collect the data; I deliver the verdict and the evidence your team and, <a href={REGULATION}>from 2027</a>, your safety assessors will ask for.
        </p>
        <p class="ask">
          <a class="btn" href={author.cal} rel="noopener">Book a 30-minute call</a>
          <a href={mailto}>or send me one incident</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-figure">
        <p class="figure-lead">One example, on a public recording: the robot was in one corridor, and reported, sure to a few centimetres, that it was in another.</p>
        <StataPlan />
        <p class="cause">The cause: after about {offMapMinutes} minutes on a floor its map did not contain, it relocalised to the wrong corridor and stayed there.</p>
        <StataChart />
        <p class="note">A PR2 in MIT's Stata Center, from a public dataset, replayed and graded by me. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/finding-confidently-wrong.md`}>Source</a></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>If your monitoring trusts the robot's own uncertainty</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>On the recording behind that example: the check most teams write first, tuned in hindsight, against mine, at the same rate of flags on healthy poses ({base.detectors.healthy}%).</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Healthy flagged</th><th scope="col">Lost flagged</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Threshold on the localiser's own uncertainty, picked knowing the answer</td><td class="h">{base.sigma_hindsight.healthy}%</td><td class="n">{base.sigma_hindsight.lost}%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Four detectors (covariance spikes, transform jumps, disagreement with the wheels, gaps in the sensor stream), frozen before the run</td><td class="h">{base.detectors.healthy}%</td><td class="n">{base.detectors.lost}%</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="note">
          One recording, one robot, graded against the dataset's ceiling AprilTags. The {base.detectors.lost}% is an upper bound ({base.detectors_events_starting_in_lost_window}% counting only detections that start in the lost window), and {base.lost_by_neither_hindsight}% of lost poses were flagged by neither check. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/finding-confidently-wrong.md`}>Source</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If your alarms were tuned on one robot</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>Set on a simulated TurtleBot3, a covariance threshold sat inside the healthy noise of a real Tiago and fired five times on a recording with nothing wrong. A threshold belongs to the machine it was measured on, so I set yours on your recordings and measure how often each fires when nothing is wrong. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/transferability.md`}>Source</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you run Nav2, check this in one minute</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <p>Stock Nav2 ships AMCL with both recovery terms at 0.0, which leaves kidnap recovery off unless you change them. If both print 0.0, a displaced robot has no mechanism to conclude it is lost.</p>
        <pre><code>ros2 param get /amcl recovery_alpha_slow
ros2 param get /amcl recovery_alpha_fast</code></pre>
        <p class="note"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/finding-amcl-recovery.md`}>Source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/jazzy/nav2_bringup/params/nav2_params.yaml">Nav2 defaults</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <div class="body">
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><strong>You send one recording</strong> from an incident: rosbag2 or ROS 1 .bag, and a line on what the robot did.</li>
          <li><strong>I read it offline.</strong> Analysis runs on your infrastructure or under NDA on mine; nothing is retained after handover. The tool reads the bag from disk and calls nothing outside it.</li>
          <li><strong>You get a written account</strong>: what happened, what the evidence supports, and what it does not.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Before each software release</strong>, the same checks run on your recordings of the old version and the new one, and you get in writing what changed.</p>
        <p class="ask">
          <a class="btn" href={author.cal} rel="noopener">Book a 30-minute call</a>
          <a href={mailto}>or send me one incident</a>
        </p>
        <p class="mail"><a href={mailto}>{author.email}</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>
      Every number on this page recomputes from <a href={REPO}>github.com/thrmnn/ros2-localization-triage</a>. Recorded data: MIT Stata Center dataset (CC BY 3.0), Universidad de León clean-and-attack recordings (CC BY 4.0).
    </p>
    <p>Who I am, and my research on cities: <a href="https://theoalessandro.com">theoalessandro.com</a></p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page, .foot { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px; }
  .page { padding-top: 40px; color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .who { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .who strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(27px, 5.6vw, 40px); line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 24px 0 16px; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .ask { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px 20px; margin: 0; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 22px;
    background: var(--text-primary); color: var(--bg-primary); border: 2px solid var(--text-primary);
    border-radius: 0; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--bg-primary); color: var(--text-primary); }
  .hero-figure { margin-top: 40px; }
  .figure-lead { font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .cause { margin: 8px 0 20px; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .body > * + * { margin-top: 12px; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .btn, .btn:hover { text-decoration: none; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 16px; }
  th { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--text-primary); }
  th + th, td.n, td.h { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; padding-left: 16px; }
  td.h { font-size: 18px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  td.n { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
  .hero-figure .note { margin-top: 6px; }
  pre { padding: 12px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--border); overflow-x: auto; font: 14px/1.5 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: step; padding: 0; }
  .steps li { counter-increment: step; position: relative; padding-left: 36px; }
  .steps li + li { margin-top: 12px; }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(step); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 2px; width: 24px; height: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--text-primary); font: 700 13px/22px 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; text-align: center; }
  #contact .ask { margin-top: 24px; }
  .mail { font-size: 16px; }
  .foot { padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 40px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); }

  /* Laptop and up: the type column stays readable, the figure and the section
     labels use the width instead of leaving two empty margins. */
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .page, .foot { max-width: 68rem; padding: 0 48px; }
    .page { padding-top: 64px; }
    .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 22rem; column-gap: 64px; align-items: end; }
    .who { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    h1 { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 2; font-size: 44px; margin: 28px 0 0; }
    .hero-side { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; }
    .hero-figure { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 3; margin-top: 48px; max-width: 44rem; }
    section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 18rem 1fr; column-gap: 64px; margin-top: 64px; padding-top: 40px; }
    section h2 { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .body { max-width: 40rem; }
    .foot p { max-width: 40rem; margin-left: calc(18rem + 64px); }
    .foot p + p { margin-top: 8px; }
  }
</style>
